module nfkbActivationDetection
module immunofluorescenceDetection

manifest NIH3T3_p65dsRed_H2BGFP_Cells
manifest FibronectinCoating
manifest PBS
manifest FluoroBriteDMEM_TNFalpha
manifest ParaformaldehydeFixative
manifest BlockingPermeabilizationBuffer
manifest IkBa_PrimaryAntibody
manifest AlexaFluor647_SecondaryAntibody

instructions:

// ============================================================
// Computer Vision Reveals Hidden Variables Underlying
// NF-kB Activation in Single Cells
// Patel, Drayman, Liu, Bilgic, Tay - Sci. Adv. 2021; 7: eabg4135
// DOI: 10.1126/sciadv.abg4135
//
// Protocol: High-throughput microfluidic live-cell imaging of
// mouse NIH 3T3 fibroblasts expressing p65-dsRed and H2B-GFP
// reporters, TNF-alpha stimulation, single-cell NF-kB nuclear
// translocation tracking, and fixed-cell immunofluorescence
// validation of the IkB/NF-kB ratio as the primary determinant
// of heterogeneous single-cell activation.
//
// CELL LINE: Knockout p65(-/-) mouse NIH 3T3 fibroblasts
//   re-engineered with p65-dsRed under native p65 promotor and
//   ubiquitin-promotor-driven H2B-GFP (nuclear marker).
//   Minimum fluorescence clone selected for endogenous NF-kB
//   expression levels. (Materials and Methods, paper p. 8)
//
// MICROFLUIDIC DEVICE: PDMS chambers coated with fibronectin
//   (FC010-10MG) overnight. Cells seeded at ~20,000 cells/cm2
//   and cultured for 5 h before stimulation at 37 C / 5% CO2.
//   TNF-alpha vials pressurized at 5 psi, connected via PEEK
//   microbore tubing (VICI). Device mounted on Nikon Eclipse Ti2
//   microscope with Hamamatsu ORCA-Flash4.0 V3 Digital CMOS
//   camera (C13440), 20x magnification, 5 min imaging interval.
//
// STIMULATION: TNF-alpha (PMC3014_3671982503) diluted in
//   FluoroBrite DMEM (A1896701) with 2x GlutaMAX (35050061),
//   penicillin/streptomycin (15140-122), and FBS (16140071).
//   Final concentration: 0.1 ng/mL for main single-dose dataset
//   (n = 2113 cells). Multi-dose dataset: 0.005, 0.05, 0.5,
//   5 ng/mL (n = 3456 cells total). (Materials and Methods, p. 8)
//
// ACTIVATION LABELING: NF-kB activation quantified as mean
//   nuclear fluorescence intensity (background corrected).
//   Peak analysis: MATLAB smooth + z-score normalization,
//   then peak detection. Binary activation label: nuclear
//   p65_peak - nuclear p65_(t=0) > 500 threshold. (Fig. S4A)
//   Activated cells show complete cytoplasm-to-nucleus p65
//   translocation in digital (switch-like) fashion. (Fig. 1D)
//
// MACHINE LEARNING: Image-based SVM (cubic kernel, 73% accuracy
//   on full multi-dose dataset; 79.4% on single-dose independent
//   validation set, n = 2113). 236 hand-crafted features per
//   cell including nuclear p65-dsRed level, SD, phase texture
//   (entropy, pixel correlation, information measure),
//   Otsu dimension, SFTA. Top predictor: mean nuclear p65-dsRed
//   prestimulation level (r = 0.62 with activation probability).
//   (Results section, paper pp. 2-4; table S1; fig. S4)
//
// FIXED-CELL IMMUNOFLUORESCENCE: Validates IkBa/NF-kB ratio
//   as activation probability determinant. Primary: rabbit
//   polyclonal anti-IkB-alpha (ab7217). Secondary: goat
//   polyclonal anti-rabbit IgG H&L Alexa Fluor 647 (G378361).
//   Imaging at time point immediately preceding fixation (5 min
//   before fixation) for UMAP alignment. (Materials and Methods)
//
// DURATION TOKENS: BioScript supports s and m only.
//   No h token. 5 h culture = 300m. Overnight fibronectin
//   coating = 720m. 1.5 h prestimulation imaging = 90m.
//   6 h post-stimulation imaging = 360m.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main               -- device prep, cell seeding, culture,
//                              prestimulation imaging, TNF stimulation,
//                              post-stimulation imaging, QC detection
//   BB2  activationPass     -- activationSignal > 0: NF-kB activated
//                              (p65 peak threshold exceeded); proceed
//                              to fixed-cell immunofluorescence
//   BB3  activationFail     -- activationSignal <= 0: non-responding
//                              cell; drain unstained cell droplet
//   BB4  activationJoin     -- join: IkBa staining branch begins
//   BB5  stainingPass       -- ifStainingSignal > 0: IkB/NF-kB ratio
//                              quantified; dispose stained sample
//   BB6  stainingFail       -- ifStainingSignal <= 0: staining failed;
//                              drain stained sample
//   BB7  finalCleanup       -- terminal: dispose QC signals; end
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Coat PDMS microfluidic chamber with fibronectin
//         (FC010-10MG) overnight at room temperature to
//         promote cell adhesion. Overnight = 720m (12 h;
//         paper states "coated with fibronectin overnight").
//         This models the surface functionalization step
//         prior to cell loading.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectinSolution = dispense 1 units of FibronectinCoating
coatedChamber       = mix fibronectinSolution with fibronectinSolution for 720m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Wash unbound fibronectin with PBS before cell
//         seeding. 1-min PBS wash to remove excess coating.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsWash1    = dispense 1 units of PBS
chamberwash = mix coatedChamber with pbsWash1 for 1m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Seed NIH 3T3 p65-dsRed / H2B-GFP reporter cells
//         into the fibronectin-coated microfluidic chamber.
//         Density: ~20,000 cells/cm2. Cells taken at 100%
//         confluence via 0.25% trypsin-ETDA (25200-056) for
//         5 min before loading (off-chip; modelled as part
//         of the cell dispense step here).
//         Culture conditions: 5% CO2, 37 C, 5 h before
//         stimulation (= 300m).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

cellSuspension  = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_p65dsRed_H2BGFP_Cells
seededChamber   = mix chamberwash with cellSuspension for 5s

// 5-hour pre-stimulation culture at 37 C / 5% CO2.
// Cells allowed to adhere and equilibrate to endogenous
// p65-dsRed / H2B-GFP expression levels before imaging.
heat seededChamber at 37c for 300m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Prestimulation imaging (1.5 h = 90m).
//         Phase and fluorescence images captured every 5 min
//         at 20x magnification. p65-dsRed (red) and H2B-GFP
//         (green) channels acquired simultaneously.
//         This unperturbed imaging window provides the input
//         feature set for the SVM classifier (236 features
//         per cell, including nuclear p65 level, texture,
//         H2B morphology). Images fed to machine learning
//         pipeline for prestimulation activation prediction.
//         (Fig. 1C-E; Results section p. 2)
//
//         NOTE: mix models the imaging acquisition loop
//         (repeated field-of-view capture over 90 min).
//         No reagent mixing occurs at this step.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsImaging      = dispense 1 units of PBS
prestimImaging  = mix seededChamber with pbsImaging for 90m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: TNF-alpha stimulation at 0.1 ng/mL.
//         TNF-alpha diluted in FluoroBrite DMEM + 2x GlutaMAX
//         + penicillin/streptomycin + FBS. Vial pressurized
//         at 5 psi; stimulus delivered via PEEK microbore
//         tubing. Stimulation marks t = 0 for all trace
//         analyses. (Materials and Methods, paper p. 8)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tnfStimulus     = dispense 1 units of FluoroBriteDMEM_TNFalpha
stimulatedCells = mix prestimImaging with tnfStimulus for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Post-stimulation live-cell imaging (6 h = 360m).
//         Cells imaged every 5 min. Nuclear NF-kB (p65-dsRed)
//         translocation tracked in real time per cell.
//         Activated cells: rapid cytoplasm-to-nucleus p65
//         translocation (digital / switch-like, within
//         ~40 min of stimulation). Non-responding cells:
//         no translocation, no target gene expression.
//         Custom MATLAB scripts: background correction,
//         smooth + z-score normalization, peak detection.
//         Activation label: binary threshold on p65_peak
//         - p65_(t=0) > 500. (Fig. 1C-D; Fig. S4A)
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat stimulatedCells at 37c for 360m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: NF-kB activation QC detection.
//         nfkbActivationDetection module abstracts the MATLAB
//         image analysis pipeline: nuclear segmentation,
//         mean nuclear fluorescence extraction, peak height
//         computation, and binary label assignment per cell.
//         Detection window: 30 s (represents the final image
//         analysis classification step at end of experiment).
//         Signal > 0: activated cell (p65 peak exceeded
//         threshold of 500; nuclear translocation confirmed).
//         Signal <= 0: non-responding cell.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

activationSignal = detect nfkbActivationDetection on stimulatedCells for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Activation QC gate
// Pass (BB2): activationSignal > 0 -> NF-kB activated cell
//             identified; proceed to fixed-cell IF staining
//             to validate IkB/NF-kB ratio hypothesis.
// Fail (BB3): activationSignal <= 0 -> non-responding cell;
//             drain (no downstream staining required).
// Both branches converge at BB4 (activationJoin).
// ============================================================

if (activationSignal > 0) {
    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 8 (Pass path): Fix cells for immunofluorescence.
    //   PBS rinse (1 min), then 4% paraformaldehyde (PFA)
    //   fixation for 10 min at room temperature (25 C).
    //   Fixation captures the cellular state immediately
    //   before fixation (images taken at t = -5 min used
    //   for UMAP alignment with live imaging data).
    //   (Materials and Methods - Fixed-cell IF, paper p. 8)
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    pbsRinse        = dispense 1 units of PBS
    rinsedCells     = mix stimulatedCells with pbsRinse for 1m

    pfaSolution     = dispense 1 units of ParaformaldehydeFixative
    fixedCells      = mix rinsedCells with pfaSolution for 10m

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 9 (Pass path): Block and permeabilize.
    //   10% BSA + 0.5% Triton X-100 in PBS for 1 h at
    //   room temperature (25 C). Blocks non-specific antibody
    //   binding and permeabilizes cell membranes to allow
    //   access of antibodies to intracellular IkB-alpha.
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    blockingBuffer      = dispense 1 units of BlockingPermeabilizationBuffer
    blockedCells        = mix fixedCells with blockingBuffer for 60m

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 10 (Pass path): Primary antibody incubation.
    //   Anti-IkB-alpha rabbit polyclonal (ab7217) in staining
    //   solution (2% BSA + 0.1% Triton X-100 in PBS) for
    //   1 h at 37 C. IkB-alpha is the main inhibitor of
    //   NF-kB (p65), sequestering it in the cytoplasm of
    //   unstimulated cells. The IkB/NF-kB ratio is the
    //   primary molecular determinant of p65 leakiness and
    //   thus activation probability (Fig. 4; Fig. 5).
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    primaryAntibody     = dispense 1 units of IkBa_PrimaryAntibody
    primaryStained      = mix blockedCells with primaryAntibody for 60m
    heat primaryStained at 37c for 60m

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 11 (Pass path): PBS wash to remove unbound
    //   primary antibody before secondary incubation.
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    pbsWash2            = dispense 1 units of PBS
    washedCells         = mix primaryStained with pbsWash2 for 1m

    // --------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 12 (Pass path): Secondary antibody incubation.
    //   Goat polyclonal anti-rabbit IgG H&L Alexa Fluor 647
    //   (G378361) in staining solution for 1 h at 37 C.
    //   Alexa Fluor 647: excitation ~650 nm, emission ~668 nm.
    //   Enables quantification of IkB-alpha protein levels
    //   in nuclear and cytoplasmic compartments by
    //   immunofluorescence for IkB/NF-kB ratio analysis.
    //   (Materials and Methods; Fig. 5A-D, paper pp. 6-7)
    // --------------------------------------------------------

    secondaryAntibody   = dispense 1 units of AlexaFluor647_SecondaryAntibody
    stainedCells        = mix washedCells with secondaryAntibody for 60m
    heat stainedCells at 37c for 60m

    dispose stainedCells
} else {
    drain stimulatedCells
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: activationJoin
// Dispose activation QC signal. Control falls into the
// immunofluorescence staining QC branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose activationSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 13: Immunofluorescence staining QC detection.
//   immunofluorescenceDetection module abstracts the image
//   analysis step for fixed cells: nuclear and cytoplasmic
//   segmentation of Alexa Fluor 647 signal (IkB-alpha),
//   p65-dsRed channel quantification, and computation of
//   the IkB/NF-kB ratio per cell.
//   Validation outcome: significant inverse correlation
//   between IkB/NF-kB ratio and leaky nuclear p65
//   (rho = -0.256, P = 2.7e-11; Fig. 5C). Activated
//   (high-scoring) fixed cells show significantly lower
//   IkB/NF-kB ratio, higher nuclear NF-kB, and larger
//   cellular area than inactive cells (Fig. 5D).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

pbsFinalWash        = dispense 1 units of PBS
finalSample         = mix pbsFinalWash with pbsFinalWash for 1m

ifStainingSignal    = detect immunofluorescenceDetection on finalSample for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Immunofluorescence staining QC gate
// Pass (BB5): ifStainingSignal > 0 -> IkB/NF-kB ratio
//             successfully quantified; dispose stained sample.
// Fail (BB6): ifStainingSignal <= 0 -> staining failure
//             (antibody issue or segmentation error); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (ifStainingSignal > 0) {
    dispose finalSample
} else {
    drain finalSample
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose immunofluorescence QC signal. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose ifStainingSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
